Skip translating a latin1 string in sequal() when the other string is
shorter and needs no translation, and hash strings from their first
byte.

When a character vector holds a string in a marked encoding,
duplicated(), unique() and anyDuplicated() hash and compare its
strings as UTF-8.  sequal() (src/main/unique.c) then falls back to
Seql(), which calls translateCharUTF8() on both strings for every
probe of the hash table, so a long latin1 string in a busy probe
sequence is translated again for every lookup that passes it.
shash() also skipped each string's first byte, so "" and every
one-byte string share one hash value and form one long probe run.

Translating latin1 to UTF-8 never shortens a string, so sequal() now
rejects the pair without translating when the other string is shorter
and needs no translation (ASCII, UTF-8, or native in a UTF-8 locale).
That only skips comparisons that would fail, so results do not change.
shash() now hashes from the first byte.

Found by OSS-Fuzz (libFuzzer_r_sort): testcase 6230127755984896, an
unreproducible Timeout in slot 19 (Encoding(l) <- "latin1"; ...;
unique(l); duplicated(c(l, x))).  The 7 KB input is a 2245-byte line
of mostly 0x90 and 0x96 followed by 1459 empty lines; the long line
hashes into the run of empty and one-byte strings and is translated
for each of their lookups.  R 4.6.1 takes 0.25 s in unique(l) and
0.48 s in duplicated(c(l, x)); under ASan each translation's buffer
allocation pushed the slot past 25 s.  With this patch both take
about 1 ms.

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #499, filed 2026-11-16; no R
Bugzilla report yet.  The upstream PR also adds a regression test to
tests/reg-fuzz.R, left out here so this carry patch does not go stale
with that file.
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk.

diff --git a/src/main/unique.c b/src/main/unique.c
index 8ad8ab2059..dce5feb57f 100644
--- a/src/main/unique.c
+++ b/src/main/unique.c
@@ -219,7 +219,7 @@ static R_INLINE hlen shash(SEXP x, R_xlen_t indx, HashData *d)
 	const void *vmax = vmaxget();
 	p = noTrans ? CHAR(xi) : translateCharUTF8(xi);
 	k = 0;
-	while (*p++)
+	for (; *p; p++)
 	    /* multiplier was 8 but 11 isn't a power of 2 */
 	    k = 11 * k + (unsigned int) *p;
 	vmaxset(vmax); /* discard any memory used by translateChar */
@@ -230,7 +230,7 @@ static R_INLINE hlen shash(SEXP x, R_xlen_t indx, HashData *d)
     /* Not having d->useCache really should not happen anymore. */
     p = translateCharUTF8(STRING_ELT(x, indx));
     k = 0;
-    while (*p++)
+    for (; *p; p++)
 	k = 11 * k + (unsigned int) *p; /* was 8 but 11 isn't a power of 2 */
     vmaxset(vmax); /* discard any memory used by translateChar */
     return scatter(k, d);
@@ -300,6 +300,15 @@ static R_INLINE int sequal(SEXP x, R_xlen_t i, SEXP y, R_xlen_t j)
     /* another pre-test to avoid the call to Seql */
     if (IS_CACHED(xi) && IS_CACHED(yj) && ENC_KNOWN(xi) == ENC_KNOWN(yj))
 	return 0;
+    /* Translating latin1 to UTF-8 never shortens a string, so a shorter
+       string that needs no translation (ASCII, UTF-8, or native in a
+       UTF-8 locale) cannot equal it: this spares translating a long
+       latin1 string on every probe past it. */
+    if (IS_LATIN1(xi) != IS_LATIN1(yj)) {
+	SEXP l = IS_LATIN1(xi) ? xi : yj, o = IS_LATIN1(xi) ? yj : xi;
+	if (LENGTH(o) < LENGTH(l) && (utf8locale || IS_ASCII(o) || IS_UTF8(o)))
+	    return 0;
+    }
     return Seql(xi, yj);
 }
 
